---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Stage from "../../components/Stage.astro";
---
<Base title="Table: scrollable and stacked layouts" description="iVOLT table: scrollable wrapper, striped, compact and bordered modifiers, and a stacked layout for narrow screens. No data engine.">
  <article class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Table</h1>
    <p>Styles for real <code>&lt;table&gt;</code> markup: caption, header cells with <code>scope</code>, and a wrapper that scrolls horizontally when the table is wider than its container. There is no sorting, filtering or data engine.</p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>CSS:</strong> <code>css/components/table.css</code> (in <code>ivolt.css</code>).</p>
    <Section title="Scrollable wrapper" num={1} lead={`iv-table-wrap is a labelled, focusable region (role="region", tabindex="0") so keyboard users can scroll it.`}>
      <Stage primary name="table/basic" title="A table in its scrollable wrapper" />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Stacked on small screens" num={2} lead={`iv-table--stack turns each row into a block below the md breakpoint and prints data-iv-label before each cell.`}>
      <Stage name="table/stack" title="Stacked on a narrow screen" />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Modifiers" num={3} lead={`--striped, --compact, --bordered, --stack. Numeric columns use iv-u-text-end.`}>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Common mistakes" num={4}>
      <ul><li>Tables used for layout.</li><li>Header cells without <code>scope</code>.</li><li>Stacked tables without <code>data-iv-label</code> on cells.</li></ul>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Class index" num={5}>
      <p>Parts and modifiers of this family that the examples above do not show. The full list per stylesheet lives in the <a href="/reference">reference</a>.</p>
      <div class="docs-scroller docs-class-index">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>iv-table--striped</code></td><td>Zebra rows.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>iv-table--bordered</code></td><td>Border on every cell.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>iv-table--compact</code></td><td>Tighter padding for dense data.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Base>
